.nh
.TH "BCDOCK" "1" "Jan 2025" "BCDock CLI" "BCDock Manual"

.SH NAME
bcdock-auth-keys - List and revoke your company's API keys


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbcdock auth keys [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List and revoke the API keys of your active company.

.PP
Keys are created in the portal (Profile -> API keys), or by 'bcdock auth login'.
A key cannot create keys, but any key of the company can list and revoke them,
so a leaked key can be revoked from the CLI.

.PP
Exit codes:
  0   ok
  1   general error


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for keys


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env: BCDOCK_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colored output

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, csv

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Request timeout

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	API token (env: BCDOCK_TOKEN)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  bcdock auth keys list
  bcdock auth keys revoke <id>
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbcdock-auth(1)\fP, \fBbcdock-auth-keys-list(1)\fP, \fBbcdock-auth-keys-revoke(1)\fP
